            <ArticleTitle>Meckel's diverticulum incarcerated in an umbilical hernia--case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>386-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2478/v10035-011-0061-1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hernias containing incarcerated Meckel's diverticulum are rare and often asymptomatic. The proper preoperative diagnosis is difficult to establish. The presence of a Meckel's diverticulum incarcerated in a hernia should be consider in a differential diagnosis of abdominal disease that is not sufficiently apparent. We present a case of a 22 years old male patient with a Meckel's diverticulum incarcerated in an umbilical hernia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
